# 8. Implement Graph-Guided Retrieval

This is one of the most important improvements.

Do not treat Neo4j and Qdrant as completely independent retrieval systems.

Use initial retrieval to identify candidate symbols, then use Neo4j to expand the candidates.

Example:

```text
Query:
"How does processOrder validate a customer?"
```

Initial vector/lexical retrieval:

```text
processOrder()
```

Graph expansion:

```text
processOrder
    |
    +-- CALLS --> validateCustomer
    |
    +-- CALLS --> validateOrder
    |
    +-- CALLS --> calculateInterest
    |
    +-- CALLS --> saveOrder
```

Retrieve source code for the relevant graph neighbors.

Graph relationships to support:

```text
CALLS
USES
INJECTS
IMPLEMENTS
EXTENDS
ACCEPTS
RETURNS
TESTED_BY
```

Also include cross-repository relationships.

