# 10. Add Parent / Neighbor Context Expansion

When a vector result identifies a chunk, retrieve its surrounding context.

For example:

```text
chunk 3
```

may expand to:

```text
chunk 2
chunk 3
chunk 4
```

Where possible, prefer AST-aware expansion over arbitrary token windows.

Expansion hierarchy:

```text
chunk
  |
  +--> parent method
  |
  +--> class
  |
  +--> sibling method
  |
  +--> caller
  |
  +--> callee
```

Make expansion configurable.

Example:

```properties
rag.context-expansion.enabled=true
rag.context-expansion.neighbor-chunks=1
rag.context-expansion.include-parent=true
rag.context-expansion.include-siblings=false
rag.context-expansion.include-callers=true
rag.context-expansion.include-callees=true
```

Do not expand everything automatically.

Use query intent to determine expansion.

