# 49. Add Graph Consistency Checks

Periodically validate:

```text
CALLS target exists
USES target exists
INJECTS target exists
IMPLEMENTS target exists
EXTENDS target exists
```

Detect:

```text
orphan nodes
STUB nodes
stale relationships
duplicate relationships
missing cross-repo links
```

Expose this through diagnostics.

---

# 50. Add Retrieval Quality / Confidence Guardrails

If retrieval confidence is low:

```text
do not confidently answer
```

Instead provide the LLM with:

```text
confidence = LOW
```

and require it to state uncertainty.

Example:

```text
High confidence:
exact symbol + AST relationship + source

Medium:
vector + graph

Low:
semantic-only match
```

This reduces hallucination.

---

# 51. Preserve Deterministic Retrieval Where Possible

The system should follow this principle:

```text
Deterministic information
        ↓
AST / Neo4j

Semantic information
        ↓
Vector / reranker

Synthesis
        ↓
LLM
```

Do not use the LLM to determine relationships that AST/Neo4j can determine exactly.

Examples:

```text
Who calls method X?
    -> Neo4j

What class implements interface X?
    -> Neo4j

Where is method X?
    -> Neo4j

How does this business flow work?
    -> Hybrid + LLM

Why might this failure occur?
    -> Hybrid + LLM
```

