# Important Implementation Rules

1. **First inspect the existing code.**
2. Do not rewrite working services unnecessarily.
3. Reuse existing `QueryIntentClassifier`.
4. Reuse existing `AdaptiveRetrievalRouter`.
5. Reuse existing Neo4j graph relationships.
6. Reuse existing Qdrant metadata.
7. Reuse the existing TEI reranker.
8. Reuse existing source-line retrieval.
9. Reuse existing incremental ingestion/hash mechanisms.
10. Preserve MCP compatibility.
11. Preserve existing API contracts unless there is a strong reason to change them.
12. Avoid introducing a new framework when an existing dependency already provides the functionality.
13. Keep retrieval strategies independently testable.
14. Keep ranking configurable.
15. Keep graph traversal bounded.
16. Keep LLM usage out of deterministic code-analysis operations.
17. Do not blindly increase `topK`.
18. Do not blindly lower similarity thresholds.
19. Do not blindly increase embedding/reranking concurrency.
20. Measure retrieval quality before and after each major change.

